## 2. Deterministic Security Sign-Off Table (`SR11`, `SR12`)

Findings use the unified 3-tier severity scale **`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`; never use `CRITICAL`/`HIGH`/`MEDIUM`/`LOW` or `P0`–`P3`):

| Finding State on Review Revision | Security Sign-Off Verdict | Required Next Step |
|---|---|---|
| **Any `CONFIRMED BLOCKER` or `CONFIRMED MAJOR`** | **`CHANGES_REQUESTED`** | Code Writer fixes root cause and reruns verification gates |
| **Any `PLAUSIBLE BLOCKER` or `PLAUSIBLE MAJOR`** | **`BLOCKED`** | Provide the named missing test or code-path evidence to confirm or refute |
| **`MINOR` findings only (zero `BLOCKER`/`MAJOR`)** | **`APPROVED`** | Findings recorded in report; fixed when low-risk or tracked |
| **Zero security findings** | **`APPROVED`** | Sign off with `"0 security findings on revision <sha>"` |

